.TH LIKEOS-EXPLORER 1 "October 2026" "LikeOS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
likeos-explorer \- browse and manage files and folders
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B likeos-explorer
.RI [ location ...]
.br
.B likeos-explorer \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B likeos-explorer
is File Explorer, the desktop's file manager: the window a folder opens in
from the desktop, the Programs menu, the window manager's menu and any
program that opens a folder (\fBxdg-open\fR).  The desktop itself stays
PCManFM's.
.PP
Each invocation opens a window, with a tab for every
.I location
given, or Home when none is.  A location is a folder (a path, a URI or
.BR ~/ ...),
a file (its folder opens with the file selected),
.B trash:///
for the Trash,
.B computer:///
for This PC, or
.B likeos:home
for Home.  A second invocation hands its locations to the running program
over the session bus, so all windows share one list of file operations,
one undo history and one clipboard.
.SH THE WINDOW
.TP
.B Tabs
Each tab is a place of its own with its own history.
.TP
.B Navigation bar
Back, Forward (right-click for the history), Up and Refresh; the address
bar, whose crumbs open their folder and whose arrows list the folders
inside, and which turns into a text field on a click beside the crumbs;
and the search box, which searches the folder shown and everything below
it.
.TP
.B Command bar
New, Cut, Copy, Paste, Rename, Share, Delete, Sort, View, and more behind
the three dots.  What the selection does not allow is greyed out.  In the
Trash it offers Empty Trash, Restore and Restore all.
.TP
.B Navigation pane
Home, the personal folders, Pinned (the GTK bookmarks, shared with every
file dialog), This PC with its drives, Network when a backend provides
it, and the Trash.  Files dropped on a row are copied or moved there.
.TP
.B Content
Home shows the pinned folders, the frequently used folders, Favorites,
the recently used files and the other places.  This PC shows the drives
with their free space.  A folder is shown as Details, List, Compact, Icons,
Large icons (with thumbnails) or Tiles; the choice is remembered per
folder.
.TP
.B Details and preview panes
The selected item's picture, type, size, dates and place, or its contents:
an image, the beginning of a text, a video's frame and length.
.SS Searching
Words in the search box must all appear in a name; case does not matter.
.B *
and
.B ?
match any characters.
.B kind:image
(or video, audio, document, folder, archive, program) and
.B ext:png
filter by kind and extension.  Below the home folder an index answers at
once; elsewhere the folders are searched as the results come in.
.SH KEYS
.TS
l l.
Ctrl+T, Ctrl+W, Ctrl+N	new tab, close tab, new window
Alt+Left, Alt+Right, Alt+Up	back, forward, up
Ctrl+L, Alt+D, F4	edit the address
Ctrl+F, Ctrl+E, F3	search
F5	refresh
Ctrl+X, Ctrl+C, Ctrl+V	cut, copy, paste
Ctrl+Shift+C	copy the path
F2	rename
Delete	move to the Trash
Shift+Delete	delete permanently
Ctrl+Shift+N	new folder
Ctrl+Z, Ctrl+Y	undo, redo
Ctrl+A	select all
Alt+Enter	properties
Alt+P, Alt+Shift+P	preview pane, details pane
Ctrl+H	show hidden items
Ctrl+Shift+2...8	the views of the View menu
Ctrl+wheel	smaller or larger view
.TE
.PP
Typing a name in a folder selects the first item that starts with it.
.SH FILE OPERATIONS
Copies, moves, deletions and the rest run in the background, at most two
at a time and never two into the same folder at once.  An operation that
takes more than a moment opens the
.B File operations
window, which shows each one's progress, speed and time left and can
cancel it.
.PP
When a name is taken at the destination, Explorer asks whether to replace
the existing item, skip, keep both (the new item gets a number), or for two
folders merge them, with a choice to answer the same way for the rest.  A
failure can be retried, skipped or the whole operation cancelled.
.PP
A file is copied under a hidden temporary name and renamed into place when
complete, so an interrupted or cancelled copy leaves no half-written file.
A move between drives removes the original only when all of it arrived.
.PP
Undo reverses the last copy, move, rename, new item, move to the Trash or
restore: copies and new items go to the Trash, moved and renamed items go
back, trashed items are restored.  Deleting permanently and emptying the
Trash cannot be undone.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/Trash
The Trash (freedesktop.org layout).
.TP
.I ~/.config/gtk-3.0/bookmarks
Pinned folders.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/recently-used.xbel
Recently used files, shared by every program.  Folder options can turn
their display off or clear the list.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/thumbnails
Thumbnails, shared with the desktop.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/likeos-explorer/index-v1
The search index of the home folder.  Turned off in Folder options, it is
deleted.
.TP
.I ~/.config/glib-2.0/settings/keyfile
Settings (schema
.BR org.likeos.Explorer ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pcmanfm (1),
.BR gio (1)
